abstract: >-
  WaterPaths-WSS extends the WaterPaths stochastic simulation and optimization
  framework with an explicit Water Supply System (WSS) layer, allowing a single
  utility to manage several hydraulically distinct subsystems, each with its own
  demands, sources, risk-of-failure triggers, drought-mitigation instruments,
  infrastructure pathway, finances, reliability and affordability objectives.
  It is configured for the two CAESB subsystems (Descoberto and Torto/Santa Maria)
  of the Federal District of Brazil.
